@style(IDocDemo)
@title(Text)

Bold, italic, colour, size, fonts, links, footnotes and other inline marks.

@section(Inline marks)

@subsection(@@b)

Bold text — b{like this}.

@b{bold}

@@strong is the same: @strong{bold}.

@subsection(@@i)

Italic text.

@i{italic}

@i(the @up(Titanic) sank)
The carry is @use(huge) important @end here.

@@emph is the same: @emph{stressed}.

@@em and @@it are the same as @@i: @em{italic} and @it{italic}.

@subsection(@@u)

Underlined text — and with a look, up to end: wave, double, dotted, dashed, thick (and a colour).

@u(underlined)

@u(wave) misspelt @end

@u(double, red) total @end

@subsection(@@s)

Struck-through text.

@s(old price)

@subsection(@@sc)

Small capitals.

@sc(Example University)

@subsection(@@sub)

Subscript text (not maths): Hsub(2)O.

@subsection(@@sup)

Superscript text (not maths): 1sup(st), xsup(2).

@sup(th)

@subsection(@@up)

Upright text inside italics.

@subsection(@@over)

A line over the text.

@over(Q)

@subsection(@@nl)

A line break (the explicit form inside a quiz line).

@nl

@@newline is the same as @@nl: one@newline two

@subsection(@@nohyphen)

Words that are never hyphenated at a line end (a name, a product).

@nohyphen(Rivera-Okafor)

@section(Colour, highlight, size and font)

@subsection(@@color)

Coloured text, up to end.

@color(red) these words @end

@color(#1d4ed8)
…paragraphs…
@end

@color(color=#b91c1c) Named with color=. @end

@subsection(@@hl)

Highlighted text.

@hl(important)

@hl(#bbf7d0) these words @end

@hl(color=#fecaca) A red highlight, set with color=. @end

@subsection(@@size)

Text at another size, up to end: 14pt, 1.2em, large, small.

@size(large) these words @end

@size(9pt)
…paragraphs…
@end

@size(size=large) Bigger words by size=. @end

@size(small) small @end and @size(huge) huge @end

@subsection(@@font)

Set the typeface for some words, the rest of a paragraph, or a whole block — and its weight (w=100–900 or light/semibold/black), letter spacing (track=0.05em) and figures (nums=oldstyle, lining, tabular, proportional).

@font(Georgia){these words}

@font(w=semibold, track=0.05em) these words @end

@font(nums=oldstyle tabular) 1234 @end

@font(Times New Roman){Times New Roman for these words}

@font(Palatino)  … @end

@font(Arial, 14pt)
text@footnote{the note}

@font(name=Georgia, size=14pt, text=Named arguments for font size and text.)

@font(weight=bold, tracking=0.08em) Bold and tracked. @end

@font(liga=false) office, flour, affix: no ligatures. @end

@section(Alignment)

@subsection(@@center)

Centre a block of content.

@center
content
@end

@subsection(@@left)

Left-align a block.

@left … @end

@subsection(@@right)

Right-align a block.

@right … @end

@subsection(@@justify)

Justify a block (flush both edges).

@justify … @end

@subsection(@@dropcap)

A large first letter sunk through the opening lines of its paragraph (3 by default; lines=2 to 6).

@dropcap(O)nce upon a time…

@dropcap(T, lines=2)he chapter opens…

@section(Notes and links)

@subsection(@@footnote)

A numbered footnote at the bottom of the page.

@subsection(@@margin)

A note in the right margin, beside the line it is written in — printed, at the same width and size on screen and in the PDF.

@subsection(@@todo)

A note to yourself: shown in the preview's margin while you write, left out of every PDF, Word and EPUB file automatically.

@subsection(@@link)

A hyperlink.

@link(https://example.com, click here)

@link(01-headings-and-structure.idoc, see the notes)

@link(01-headings-and-structure.idoc#keywords, the keywords)

@link(#keywords, jump to that section)


@link(url=https://example.org, text=a link by named arguments)

@link(https://example.org, text=A card with a thumbnail, img=auto, size=16em)

@subsection(@@rule)

A horizontal line across the text column — its width, thickness, colour and alignment.

@rule

@rule(w=50%, h=1pt, align=center)

@rule(color=#999)

@subsection(@@demo)

Shows a piece of IDoc twice: its source, answers masked, and what it makes under it.

@demo … @end

@subsection(@@lang)

Words in another language, up to end: hyphenated, quoted and set left to right or right to left as that language is.

@lang(de) Die Würde des Menschen @end

@lang(ar)
…paragraphs…
@end

@lang(lang=fr) Bonjour tout le monde. @end

@subsection(@@verb)

Raw text shown exactly as typed — monospace, whitespace preserved, nothing interpreted.

@verb{inline}

@verb(font=mono, size=13)
  exact text
@end

@verb(text=Exact text,   spaces kept., font=mono, size=13, color=#1f2937, bg=#f1f5f9, align=left, wrap)

@verb(A very long line that scrolls sideways on screen rather than wrapping, scroll, plain, w=300px, h=40px)

@verb(font=serif, align=center)
Centred, in a serif face.
@end

@@verbatim is the same as @@verb:
@verbatim
Exact   text.
@end

@@pre is the same as @@verb:
@pre
  indented   exactly
@end
